ory that had been removed  and then merge it with the stories as  they'd been told following the new 52 so  if it seems a little wild and murky and  just kind of a huge mess it was it and  it still is it's still just a continuity  mess but with regards to the dc rebirth  event dr fate actually had a huge role  in justice league dark under the dc  rebirth banner now for those of you guys  who didn't hear of justice league dark  it was a really really cool line of  comics that they basically split the  justice league into several teams but  justice league dark essentially focused  on like the magic and mysticism side the  darker side but this comic line actually  saw naboo possess kent nelson's body and  then trapped khalid in a vase but after  he was freed by the justice league dark  he ended up playing a key role in  helping to defeat naboo and then free  kent nelson of his control resulting in  both kent and khalid agreeing to shelve  the dr fate mantle while serving as  magical advisors to the justice league  dark team now of course that didn't  really last very long and both khalid  and kent nelson would take up the mantle  once again largely because fans just  wanted to see them come back however  kent is killed in battle with a being  that's known as the upside down man when  he essentially sacrifices himself to  produce a spell powerful enough to  weaken the upside down man which was  enough for his teammates to ultimately  defeat him this leaves khalid as the  sole doctor fate in dc comics which is  actually where we are right now that  kent nelson is not the main doctor fate  which i know probably sounds  disappointing if you are interested in  the character from dc comics and you  want to go read about kent nelson you're  not going to see him right now at least  not as dr fate but that's kind of where  we are here at the moment that's one of  the big one of the big things to contend  with here dc's continuity is a nightmare  in so many different ways so try